From fac880c71aa670366eb31bae6211c632248f4019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:51:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] eip155: report a signature not made by an EOA payer as
 invalid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

StructuredSignature::try_from_bytes treats a 64/65-byte signature that does not
recover to the payer as an EIP-1271 signature, so that smart wallets work. For
an EOA payer (no code) the signature can never be valid, but it was passed to
the transfer simulation anyway. The simulation reverted ("FiatTokenV2: invalid
signature", Permit2 InvalidSigner()) and the revert surfaced as a transport
error, i.e. HTTP 500 with unexpected_error, from both /verify and /settle.

Before simulating or sending an EIP-1271 signature, check that the signer has
code; if it has none, fail with an invalid-signature error. EIP-1271 wallets
(deployed, so with code) and EIP-6492 counterfactual wallets (wrapped
signatures, a separate path) are unaffected. This costs one eth_getCode, only
on the EIP-1271 path.

The v2 exact handler reports signature failures with the code x402 v2 §9
defines for the exact scheme on EVM, invalid_exact_evm_payload_signature.
